---
// THE TRIFECTA DECK (founder 2026-08-07) — one page for Andrea Pomarico
// (Four Winds Wholeness Sanctuary) and Steve (Audacity Lab), who asked to see
// this as a single proposition rather than three separate conversations.
//
// DELIBERATELY CARRIES NO FINANCIAL CLAIM. Lichen is a 501(c)(3); "investment"
// means something specific and legally distinct, and the founder is settling
// the framing in their own document. Until that lands, this page describes what
// each party brings and what weaving together looks like — and stops short of
// any number, term, instrument or return. The ask section below is a marked
// placeholder, not an omission to be forgotten.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WeavePitch from '../../components/WeavePitch.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Four Winds · Audacity Lab · Lichen"
  description="Three organisations, one proposition: land held in trust, young people growing up alongside it, and the infrastructure that makes both repeatable."
>
  <WeavePitch partner="Four Winds & Audacity Lab">
    <Fragment slot="weave">
      <span class="eyebrow">Three organisations, one proposition</span>
      <h2 class="display h2-weave">What weaving in looks like</h2>

      <p class="wbody">
        Andrea, Steve — you&rsquo;ve each been having a version of this
        conversation with us separately. This page puts it in one place, because
        the three pieces only work as one thing.
      </p>

      <p class="wbody">
        Four Winds Wholeness Sanctuary has been consciously stewarded for over
        140 years — homesteaded in 1882, and cared for since 2011 by Andrea
        Pomarico, alongside the animals, land and healing lineage that call it
        home. Andrea is ready for its next chapter, and what we&rsquo;re
        proposing doesn&rsquo;t have a name in the current system: not a single
        buyer, but a network.
      </p>

      <ol class="wpaths">
        <li>
          <strong>Four Winds — the land.</strong> Acres, animals and years of
          documented stewardship, becoming the first property held by
          Lichen&rsquo;s Land Trust. No single owner, ever. Andrea takes her
          equity out gradually rather than through one mortgaged transaction,
          funded by the network already aligned with this place.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Audacity Lab — the young people.</strong> A think-and-do lab
          running youth programming out of Four Winds, where growing up
          alongside land, animals and a working regenerative farm helps young
          people become new-era adults — learning stewardship, reciprocity and
          collective intelligence by living them, not reading about them. The
          land stops being a site Audacity Lab visits and becomes the classroom
          it holds a permanent stake in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Lichen — the infrastructure.</strong> The legal, business and
          technology layer that makes the other two durable: the Land Trust that
          receives what&rsquo;s given and holds the ground, the Current-cy
          economy that records every contribution once it&rsquo;s stewarded —
          hay, work-trade, animal care, the people who show up — and the network
          every contributor is woven into rather than left holding a receipt.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="wbody">
        Separately, each of these is a good project that depends on someone
        staying generous. Together they&rsquo;re a structure: the land can&rsquo;t
        be sold out from under the programming, the programming has somewhere
        permanent to stand, and the contributions that keep both alive are
        counted rather than forgotten. That&rsquo;s the part worth backing —
        not one property, but the first working instance of a pattern built to
        repeat.
      </p>

      <p class="wbody">
        Lichen has already published this doctrine: land in its care operates in
        full service of community, with value flowing back to the land and the
        people who tend it. Four Winds would be the first place held in
        relationship with that framework — not a case study. The actual thing,
        and the template for what comes after it.
      </p>

      <!-- ── THE ASK ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
           Left deliberately empty. The founder is settling the structure of
           what's being offered (philanthropic support for Lichen vs
           participation in the Four Winds land trust — they are different
           instruments with different legal footing) in their own document.
           Nothing here should state or imply a number, a term or a return
           until that arrives. -->

      <p class="wbody">
        The next step is the simplest one: walk the land together, with all
        three of us in the same place at the same time, and work out the shape
        of it there.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </WeavePitch>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .h2-weave { font-size: clamp(24px, 3.5vw, 36px); margin: 4px 0 0; }
</style>
